{"data": [{"author_id": "1716573538235412480", "created_at": "2026-10-22T21:13:00.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2113378107650650245"], "entities": {"urls": [{"display_url": "x.com/Reuters/status…", "end": 285, "expanded_url": "https://twitter.com/Reuters/status/2112539398503833665", "start": 262, "url": "https://t.co/kuWv5qs0u1"}]}, "id": "2113378107650650245", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 588, "like_count": 11, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 1, "retweet_count": 1}, "referenced_tweets": [{"id": "2112539398503833665", "type": "quoted"}], "text": "As a reminder: Nvidia sells a huge number of chips to China. If we got rid of export controls, they’d make much more money.\n\nIt’s massively in Nvidia’s interests to lobby against export restrictions. It spends millions on lobbying, including on export controls. https://t.co/kuWv5qs0u1", "url": "https://x.com/TheMidasProj/status/2113378107650650245"}, {"attachments": {"media_keys": ["3_2113397159584243712"]}, "author_id": "1922780583886979072", "created_at": "2026-10-22T22:28:44.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2113397168732316115"], "entities": {"hashtags": [{"end": 204, "start": 195, "tag": "Oceqsabe"}, {"end": 228, "start": 205, "tag": "ArtificialIntelligence"}, {"end": 244, "start": 229, "tag": "Semiconductors"}, {"end": 262, "start": 245, "tag": "GlobalTechnology"}, {"end": 278, "start": 263, "tag": "TechInnovation"}], "urls": [{"display_url": "pic.x.com/xyxskJwVoz", "end": 302, "expanded_url": "https://x.com/oceqsabeto43761/status/2113397168732316115/photo/1", "media_key": "3_2113397159584243712", "start": 279, "url": "https://t.co/xyxskJwVoz"}]}, "id": "2113397168732316115", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 16, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "text": "Advanced chips are becoming strategic assets in the global AI race. Discover how semiconductor technology, export controls, and international competition are shaping the future of artificial...\n\n#Oceqsabe #ArtificialIntelligence #Semiconductors #GlobalTechnology #TechInnovation https://t.co/xyxskJwVoz", "url": "https://x.com/oceqsabeto43761/status/2113397168732316115"}, {"attachments": {"media_keys": ["13_2113532183386460160"]}, "author_id": "2104232770872774656", "created_at": "2026-10-23T07:26:25.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2113532478720012542"], "entities": {"hashtags": [{"end": 247, "start": 244, "tag": "AI"}], "urls": [{"display_url": "pic.x.com/JTe3P5mv7O", "end": 271, "expanded_url": "https://x.com/doptonin/status/2113532478720012542/video/1", "media_key": "13_2113532183386460160", "start": 248, "url": "https://t.co/JTe3P5mv7O"}]}, "id": "2113532478720012542", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 3, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "text": "China just open-sourced a 293B-parameter AI monster — Spark X2.6.\n\nIt runs on zero American chips. Only 30B params wake per token: 10% awake, 100% enough.\n\nExport controls were supposed to slow China's AI. They just forced it to get efficient. #AI https://t.co/JTe3P5mv7O", "url": "https://x.com/doptonin/status/2113532478720012542"}, {"attachments": {"media_keys": ["3_2113444986398359554"]}, "author_id": "2112571275575197696", "created_at": "2026-10-23T01:38:48.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2113444998352089261"], "entities": {"urls": [{"display_url": "pic.x.com/T0OoTf7mZ6", "end": 292, "expanded_url": "https://x.com/joinTechNexus/status/2113444998352089261/photo/1", "media_key": "3_2113444986398359554", "start": 269, "url": "https://t.co/T0OoTf7mZ6"}]}, "id": "2113444998352089261", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 1, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 1, "retweet_count": 0}, "text": "🌏 Who gets to control the future of AI?\n\nChina has proposed new export controls covering advanced technologies, including AI and semiconductors.\n\nThe story isn't just about AI models. It's also about chips, manufacturing, computing power, and global technology access. https://t.co/T0OoTf7mZ6", "url": "https://x.com/joinTechNexus/status/2113444998352089261"}, {"author_id": "77961487", "created_at": "2026-10-23T03:16:58.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2113469705835233657"], "id": "2113469705835233657", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 1, "impression_count": 682, "like_count": 3, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 1, "retweet_count": 2}, "text": "\"Taiwan's TSMC, opens new tab is exploring alternatives to rare-earth components in factory equipment, three people familiar ‌with the matter said, aiming to reduce the risk that Beijing's export controls could disrupt operations at plants that make the world's most advanced", "url": "https://x.com/aadilbrar/status/2113469705835233657"}, {"author_id": "49884453", "created_at": "2026-10-23T10:57:33.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2113585612204704038"], "entities": {"cashtags": [{"end": 5, "start": 0, "tag": "INTC"}]}, "id": "2113585612204704038", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 111, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "text": "$INTC down 8% at $85.49 after new US export controls hit robotics and automation chips. Broad semiconductor selloff. Earnings Oct 29 is the next big test.", "url": "https://x.com/mhtx_x/status/2113585612204704038"}, {"author_id": "2107858134492393472", "created_at": "2026-10-23T09:55:49.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2113570076008087590"], "entities": {"cashtags": [{"end": 246, "start": 241, "tag": "NVDA"}, {"end": 251, "start": 247, "tag": "AMD"}, {"end": 258, "start": 252, "tag": "GOOGL"}]}, "id": "2113570076008087590", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 5, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "text": "Export controls back in the AI trade this morning:\n\n- Trump admin halts program that rewarded allies for aligning with US export controls (via FirstSquawk)\n- US blacklists a China AI startup tied to stolen Google AI secrets (via ZeroHedge)\n\n$NVDA $AMD $GOOGL into the open", "url": "https://x.com/MakroWire/status/2113570076008087590"}, {"attachments": {"media_keys": ["3_2114046426980265984"]}, "author_id": "2078746113016741888", "created_at": "2026-10-24T17:30:51.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2114046977843351554"], "entities": {"urls": [{"display_url": "pic.x.com/nFccerb1VP", "end": 298, "expanded_url": "https://x.com/MedAtlanticX/status/2114046977843351554/photo/1", "media_key": "3_2114046426980265984", "start": 275, "url": "https://t.co/nFccerb1VP"}]}, "id": "2114046977843351554", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 25, "like_count": 1, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "text": "TSMC is reportedly asking suppliers whether factory-automation motors can work without rare-earth components, in discussions reported on 22 October as it seeks to reduce exposure to China's export controls.\n\nThe issue extends beyond the materials in chips: motors containing https://t.co/nFccerb1VP", "url": "https://x.com/MedAtlanticX/status/2114046977843351554"}, {"attachments": {"media_keys": ["3_2113609746850684928"]}, "author_id": "1404099729525559301", "created_at": "2026-10-23T12:33:41.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2113609805105704966"], "entities": {"urls": [{"display_url": "pic.x.com/EFRRTlp4dz", "end": 225, "expanded_url": "https://x.com/Chahatusharma/status/2113609805105704966/photo/1", "media_key": "3_2113609746850684928", "start": 202, "url": "https://t.co/EFRRTlp4dz"}]}, "id": "2113609805105704966", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 67, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "text": "Lava says it found 32 Nvidia B300 chips inside China Telecom's network.\n\nTom's Hardware reports Nvidia calls smuggling \"a drop in the bucket.\"\n\nCan export controls hold if banned chips keep turning up? https://t.co/EFRRTlp4dz", "url": "https://x.com/Chahatusharma/status/2113609805105704966"}, {"author_id": "7424642", "created_at": "2026-10-23T00:23:26.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2113426031310745738"], "entities": {"urls": [{"description": "Rare-earth magnets are used in motors that power moving parts in industrial equipment, including machinery found in highly automated factories.", "display_url": "ebx.sh/7WgMur", "end": 237, "expanded_url": "https://ebx.sh/7WgMur", "images": [{"height": 999, "url": "https://pbs.twimg.com/news_img/2113426033089064960/BgzIz15h?format=jpg&name=orig", "width": 1500}, {"height": 150, "url": "https://pbs.twimg.com/news_img/2113426033089064960/BgzIz15h?format=jpg&name=150x150", "width": 150}], "start": 214, "status": 200, "title": "TSMC seeks factory-equipment alternatives to thwart China’s rare earths grip, sources say", "unwound_url": "https://ebx.sh/7WgMur", "url": "https://t.co/Vk0HHeY6rJ"}]}, "id": "2113426031310745738", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 2662, "like_count": 1, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "text": "Taiwan's TSMC is exploring alternatives to rare-earth components in factory equipment, aiming to reduce the risk that Beijing's export controls could disrupt operations at plants that make the most advanced chips. https://t.co/Vk0HHeY6rJ", "url": "https://x.com/japantimes/status/2113426031310745738"}, {"attachments": {"media_keys": ["3_2113659284529565696"]}, "author_id": "2423290023", "created_at": "2026-10-23T15:50:41.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2113659384123269139"], "entities": {"urls": [{"display_url": "pic.x.com/NoTAYfoko2", "end": 300, "expanded_url": "https://x.com/AIGovernor01/status/2113659384123269139/photo/1", "media_key": "3_2113659284529565696", "start": 277, "url": "https://t.co/NoTAYfoko2"}]}, "id": "2113659384123269139", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 278, "like_count": 2, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 2, "r