, "reply_count": 1, "retweet_count": 0}, "text": "🚨 $TSM | SUPPLY-CHAIN WATCH 🚨\n\nReuters reports TSMC is exploring rare-earth-free motors for factory equipment as China's export controls raise supply risks.\n\nThis is not yet a completed switch, but it's something to note. Advanced chips depend on rare-earth magnets.", "url": "https://x.com/QubitEconomist/status/2113610137047040103"}, {"attachments": {"media_keys": ["3_2113414953025810432"]}, "author_id": "146108201", "created_at": "2026-10-22T23:39:33.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2113414990858448948"], "entities": {"urls": [{"display_url": "pic.x.com/RuWsZUee4X", "end": 296, "expanded_url": "https://x.com/Tesla_Optimus_K/status/2113414990858448948/photo/1", "media_key": "3_2113414953025810432", "start": 273, "url": "https://t.co/RuWsZUee4X"}]}, "id": "2113414990858448948", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 37, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "text": "OpenAI, Anthropic, and Nvidia just posted record lobbying quarters\n\nJuly through September: Nvidia $2.2 million, Anthropic $2.1 million, OpenAI $1.5 million — each firm's biggest quarter. Combined almost $6 million. Microsoft already does $2 million-plus a quarter; Google https://t.co/RuWsZUee4X", "url": "https://x.com/Tesla_Optimus_K/status/2113414990858448948"}, {"author_id": "1994847917769932800", "created_at": "2026-10-24T05:45:01.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2113869352042668273"], "id": "2113869352042668273", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 19, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "text": "The chip war reaches the factory motor.\n\nReuters reported on October 22 that Taiwan's TSMC has asked suppliers about factory equipment using motors without rare earths. Three sources described an effort to reduce exposure to China's export controls.\n\nThe vulnerability sits in the", "url": "https://x.com/StratFaultLine/status/2113869352042668273"}, {"attachments": {"media_keys": ["3_2113840325546713088"]}, "author_id": "2089953238951026688", "created_at": "2026-10-24T03:49:45.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2113840341875143059"], "entities": {"urls": [{"display_url": "pic.x.com/1MeOROtSnj", "end": 295, "expanded_url": "https://x.com/tchsignal/status/2113840341875143059/photo/1", "media_key": "3_2113840325546713088", "start": 272, "url": "https://t.co/1MeOROtSnj"}]}, "id": "2113840341875143059", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 25, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 1, "retweet_count": 0}, "text": "China's AI Export Controls: Why DeepSeek and MiniMax Can Still Go Global\n\nChina is tightening oversight of AI technology exports, yet DeepSeek and MiniMax have reportedly cleared procedures to distribute AI models internationally. The two developments are not necessarily https://t.co/1MeOROtSnj", "url": "https://x.com/tchsignal/status/2113840341875143059"}, {"author_id": "1840302226046148608", "created_at": "2026-10-24T18:58:30.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2114069034714935704"], "entities": {"urls": [{"display_url": "x.com/Polymarket/sta…", "end": 145, "expanded_url": "https://twitter.com/Polymarket/status/2114053306683105486", "start": 122, "url": "https://t.co/d9JJJG8M8F"}]}, "id": "2114069034714935704", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 108, "like_count": 1, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "referenced_tweets": [{"id": "2114053306683105486", "type": "quoted"}], "text": "Export controls for the 40-ton machines. The AI edge still fits on a thumb drive and just got a one-way ticket to Riyadh. https://t.co/d9JJJG8M8F", "url": "https://x.com/JC0l3_/status/2114069034714935704"}, {"attachments": {"media_keys": ["3_2113390190207373312"]}, "author_id": "3035736060", "created_at": "2026-10-22T22:01:01.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2113390192363274423"], "entities": {"urls": [{"display_url": "pic.x.